      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "JULEP (8) has come into her own since stepping up to a middle distance, winning her last couple of starts on the bounce. She skips a couple of grades here, but will drop 3.5kg from her last win at Mortlake just over 2 weeks ago. The hat-trick beckons. SHE'S STARGAZING (6) stepped up to a middle distance third up at Kilmore last start, and ran a much better race for second. She drops 2kg, Meech sticks, and she can go one better. MICKIO (4) bolted in when scoring at Echuca at his penultimate start, and then weakened late over 2400m at Mornington a fortnight ago. He is better placed over this trip, and is worth another chance. Follow your money. LIGHTNING EXPRESS (3) will be dropping sharply in class here, and a recent jump-out suggests that he is back to something like his best. A good draw will help, and he should not be taken lightly here. MOZU MARCASSIN (7) got back after a slow start at Kilmore and never featured thereafter. He is better than that, and can make amends. Keep safe.",
